  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<section class=\"context\"><p>A bar rotates horizontally about its centre, reaching a maximum angular velocity in six complete rotations from rest. The bar has a constant angular acceleration of <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.110 rad s^{-2}\"></span>. The moment of inertia of the bar about the axis of rotation is <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"0.0216 kg m^{2}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure></p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"a\"><p><strong>a</strong> Show that the final angular velocity of the bar is about <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"3 rad s^{-1}\"></span>. [2]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"b\"><p><strong>b</strong> </p><p>Draw the variation with time <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"t\"></span> of the angular displacement <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\theta\"></span> of the bar during the acceleration.</p>\n<p><figure data-asset-id=\"fig_02\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 2\" src=\"asset:fig_02\"/></figure></p><p>[1]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"c\"><p><strong>c</strong> Calculate the torque acting on the bar while it is accelerating. [1]</p></section><section class=\"question-part\" data-label=\"d\"><p><strong>d</strong> The torque is removed. The bar comes to rest in <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"30\"></span> complete rotations with constant angular deceleration. Determine the time taken for the bar to come to rest. [2]</p></section>"
  },
